        "original_id": "82251352-873a-5e74-80e3-6a0b4c55e62d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game\n- Places: BB&T Center, Sunrise, Florida\n- Organizations: Florida Panthers, National Hockey League\n- Topics: 2002–03 NHL season, 2002–03 Florida Panthers season\n\nFacts:\n- The BB&T Center is an indoor arena in Sunrise, Florida, and it was previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center.\n- The BB&T Center was completed in 1998 at a cost of US$185 million, was financed almost entirely with public funds, and includes 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game was held during the 2002–03 NHL season on February 2, 2003, at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida.\n- The Office Depot Center was the home arena of the Florida Panthers when it hosted the 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game.\n- During the 2002–03 Florida Panthers season, the Florida Panthers did not make the playoffs but did host the 53rd All-Star Game that season.",
